## Customize flags given to the VM: https://www.erlang.org/doc/man/erl.html
## -mode/-name/-sname/-setcookie are configured via env vars, do not set them here

## Scheduler count — critical for this release.
##
## Default BEAM behavior is to auto-detect from the OS's "logical
## processors online" count. When a parent process (like Godot from
## a macOS .app bundle) spawns the release with a restricted
## sandbox, that detection can come back with 1, which collapses
## 250+ concurrent GenServers onto a single thread and stalls the
## sim within seconds.
##
## We force 16 schedulers as a ceiling that covers every realistic
## modern desktop:
##
##   - Apple Silicon M1/M2/M3/M4    → 8–12 cores, uses all
##   - Gaming PCs                    → 8–16 cores, uses all
##   - Low-end / 4-core              → BEAM spawns 16 threads but
##                                     only 4 get real CPU time;
##                                     extra threads are ~1MB stack
##                                     each and sit idle, no cost
##
## This is NOT a cap in any painful sense — scheduler threads above
## physical core count are cheap. And it means we never bottleneck
## a high-end machine on our vm.args default.
##
## Override via ERL_FLAGS="+S 32:32" in the spawn env for very
## high-core hosts (32+ cores). ERL_FLAGS wins over vm.args.
+S 16:16

## Disable the interactive shell/TTY on stdin.
##
## `bin/simulator start` normally attaches stdin to BEAM's prim_tty
## driver so you can hit ^C / evaluate expressions. When a parent
## process (Godot) spawns the release, its pipe on fd=0 isn't a real
## TTY — prim_tty still tries to claim it, and our own
## Simulator.ParentWatcher port ALSO wants fd=0 to detect EOF for
## graceful shutdown. The two fight and BEAM logs:
##
##   driver_select(...) by fd (0/2) driver Port<...> stealing
##   control of fd=0 from resource prim_tty:tty
##
## While they fight, the TTY driver can spin trying to process
## garbage from the pipe, starving a scheduler and cascading into
## tick-handler stalls. -noinput disables prim_tty entirely; our
## port becomes the sole owner of fd=0 and ParentWatcher works
## cleanly.
-noinput

## Tweak GC to run a bit more often; bounds memory with 350+ agents.
-env ERL_FULLSWEEP_AFTER 10

## Enable deployment without epmd — local-only release.
-start_epmd false
-erl_epmd_port 6789
